\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable><!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony was joined in the last line by a chorus of Elvi voices. When it was done, they cheered and applauded. Some wept openly and fully. One started snapping his fingers to the tempo Tony had settled into by the end of the second verse. Others joined in, and with a communal nod, the few who had witnessed the whole thing burst into song. They sang in unison, in keening tones straight from the vibration of their ribs and their thumping hearts.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It was perfect.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The next time they sang, more joined in, and the song spread. Every guitar on the property was found and leant to accompaniment. They sang and played until all the Elvi learned the lyrics and joined in.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>And then the performance softened and the last refrains were whispered. Silence wrapped them all in comfort. The mansion acquired the aura of a cathedral. The Elvi became one in purpose and heart. They hugged and wept.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Shedding tears, Tony laughed. He was reborn.  \'91I could really go a cheeseburger,\'92 he said to himself.
